ShortDescription: A privacy-first desktop companion of seeded procedural pixel creatures that live on your desktop.
Description: >-
  Formiga is a privacy-first desktop companion. Seeded procedural pixel creatures live in
  transparent overlays on your desktop, perch on your real windows, react to your cursor, and
  grow into a four-creature colony with a home of its own. Everything runs locally: there is no
  account system, analytics, or advertising SDK, and the only optional network feature is a
  once-a-day check for new releases that can be turned off in Settings.


  This build is unsigned, so Windows SmartScreen will warn on first run - choose "More info",
  then "Run anyway". Formiga will never ask you to disable an operating-system security feature.
